1. Scope

This licence applies to the Swoosh source code, executable builds,
documentation and project artwork distributed with this notice, to the
extent that the contributors hold the rights being licensed. These items
are referred to below as the Software. A Modified Version is a modified
copy or derivative work containing a substantial portion of the Software.
Third-party material remains subject to its own terms; this licence grants
no rights to games, keys, firmware or externally downloaded artwork.

2. Permissions

Subject to these conditions, you may use, run, study, copy, fork, modify,
build and distribute the Software and Modified Versions free of charge.
These permissions include use by businesses and other organisations and
use for commercial purposes that does not involve selling copies or rights
to the Software or a Modified Version.

You do not have to publish private changes or provide source code with a
binary distribution. Any distribution must satisfy section 3.

3. Conditions on distribution

You must provide this licence and preserve applicable copyright notices
with every distributed copy or substantial portion of the Software and
every distributed Modified Version. You must identify material changes
and must not present a Modified Version as an official Swoosh release.

The no-sale restriction in section 4 must continue to apply to the Software
and Modified Versions when they are redistributed. You may not relicense
them or grant permissions that remove that restriction. Independent code
that is not derived from the Software is outside the scope of this licence.

4. No sale of the Software or Modified Versions

You may not sell copies of the Software or a Modified Version, or charge
for the right to obtain, download, install or use such a copy. This includes
paid downloads, paid app-store listings, subscriptions that grant those
rights, and bundles used to impose a charge for the Software or a Modified
Version. Renaming the Software or changing its features does not remove
this restriction.

Free redistribution and optional donations are permitted. A donation must
not be required to obtain a copy or any of the permissions in this licence.

You may charge for separate services, such as optional support, training,
hosting or development work, provided that the Software or Modified Version
itself is supplied without a software charge under this licence. A service
fee must not be used to disguise a charge for a copy or for those rights.
This licence does not impose a general prohibition on commercial activity.

5. Other rights

These permissions are non-exclusive and conditional on compliance with
this licence. Rights not expressly granted remain with their holders.
No trademark rights or endorsement by the contributors are granted.
Nothing in this licence limits rights that applicable law gives you
independently of this licence.

6. Warranty and liability

To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Software is provided as is,
without warranties of any kind, including warranties of merchantability,
fitness for a particular purpose or non-infringement. To that same extent,
the contributors and copyright holders are not liable for claims, damages
or other liability arising from the Software or its use, whether in
contract, tort or otherwise.

